"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[75771],{375771:e=>{e.exports='# Find a Table\n\nHow to **locate relevant Lakewatch tables** by datasource, preset, or medallion layer search. Use when the user asks which table contains certain data, what tables a datasource has, or what tables are available (e.g. bronze/silver/gold).\n\nTables are not retrieved by a single ID; they are discovered via **datasource → preset → schema search**. Follow the hierarchy below. If **multiple** tables match, always present a list and **prompt the user to choose**. Use **fully qualified** names: `catalog.schema.table_name`.\n\n## Flow: Datasource → Preset → Schema search\n\n1. **Determine the datasource**\n   - User names a datasource (e.g. "CloudTrail") → get that datasource with **apiGetLakewatchResourceById** (or list then get by name).\n   - User describes data type (e.g. "authentication logs") → **apiListLakewatchDatasources**, find matching datasource(s), then get by ID.\n\n2. **Inspect datasource for tables**\n   - From the datasource response, check `spec.tables.bronze`, `spec.transforms.silver`, `spec.tables.gold` (and any `tableOverrides`).\n   - If tables are found → present them (Step 5).\n   - If none → check for `spec.preset` (name and version).\n\n3. **If preset is referenced**\n   - Call **apiGetLakewatchDatasourcePreset** with the preset name and version.\n   - Inspect preset `spec.tables` and `spec.transforms` for table definitions.\n   - If tables are found → present them.\n   - If none → continue to schema search.\n\n4. **Search medallion schemas**\n   - Use **apiGetLakewatchConfig** to get schema names (e.g. bronze, silver, gold).\n   - Call **apiGetLakewatchManagedTables** for each layer (`bronze`, `silver`, `gold`) as needed.\n   - Filter results by table name/description that match the user\'s intent.\n\n5. **Present results**\n   - **Single table** — Give fully qualified name, layer, and description; offer to help write a query.\n   - **Multiple tables** — List all with name, layer, and short description; **ask the user to choose**.\n   - **No tables** — Say what you checked (datasource, preset, schemas); suggest listing datasources or checking configuration.\n\n## User mentions a specific datasource\n\nExample: _“What tables does the CloudTrail datasource have?”_\n\n1. Get the datasource (by name or ID) with **apiGetLakewatchResourceById** (`resourceType: "datasource"`).\n2. Inspect `spec.tables` and `spec.transforms` for table definitions.\n3. If empty, check `spec.preset` and call **apiGetLakewatchDatasourcePreset**; inspect preset for tables.\n4. If still empty, use **apiGetLakewatchManagedTables** for bronze/silver/gold and filter by relevance.\n5. Present table(s); if multiple, prompt the user to choose.\n\n## User describes data type (no specific datasource)\n\nExample: _“Which table has authentication logs?”_\n\n1. **apiListLakewatchDatasources** and find datasource(s) whose name/description match (e.g. authentication).\n2. For each candidate, get with **apiGetLakewatchResourceById** and inspect for tables (Step 2–4 above).\n3. Present matches; if multiple tables or multiple datasources, list options and ask the user to choose.\n\n## User asks for "gold" / "silver" / "bronze" tables\n\nExample: _“Show me the last 10 events of CloudTrail gold table”_\n\n"Gold" (or silver/bronze) is the **medallion layer**, not part of the table name. Find CloudTrail tables in that layer:\n\n1. Get the CloudTrail datasource; inspect `spec.tables.gold` (and preset if used).\n2. Present tables in the gold layer with fully qualified names; if more than one, list and ask which to use.\n\n## Best practices\n\n- **Start from user context** — If they name a datasource, get that datasource first; avoid listing everything.\n- **Follow the hierarchy** — Datasource → Preset → Schema search; don\'t skip steps that might have the answer.\n- **Always prompt on ambiguity** — Multiple tables → present all with name, layer, description and ask the user to choose.\n- **Use fully qualified names** — Always `catalog.schema.table_name` (e.g. `lakewatch.gold.authentication_summary`).\n- **Explain medallion layers when helpful** — Bronze: raw ingested data; Silver: cleaned/enriched; Gold: aggregated/reporting.\n\n## Error handling\n\n- **Datasource not found** — Say so; offer to list available datasources or search by another name.\n- **Preset not found** — Say the datasource references a preset that couldn\'t be retrieved; offer to search medallion schemas directly.\n- **No tables found** — Summarize what was checked (datasource, preset, bronze/silver/gold); suggest checking configuration or listing datasources.\n'}}]);
